## START

1. Host System Preparation: Goal: Stable Linux base with SDN support.

	Requirements

	Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS

	16 GB (recommended)

	4 CPU cores

	Nested virtualization enabled (if using GNS3 VM later)

				sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
				sudo apt install -y curl git net-tools bridge-utils

2. Install Docker & Docker Compose: Containers minimize resource usage and improve repeatability.

				sudo apt install -y docker.io docker-compose
				sudo systemctl enable docker
				sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
				newgrp docker


	Verify:

				docker run hello-world

3. Install Open vSwitch (PEP – Network Layer): Core microsegmentation and flow enforcement.

				sudo apt install -y openvswitch-switch
				sudo systemctl start openvswitch-switch
				ovs-vsctl show

4. Install Mininet (Network Emulation): Lightweight, deterministic topology control.

				sudo apt install -y mininet
				sudo mn --test pingall

5. Deploy OpenDaylight (Policy Administrator):  Centralized SDN control translating trust decisions to flows.

				docker run -d \
				 --name opendaylight \
				 -p 8181:8181 -p 6653:6653 \
				 opendaylight/odl:latest


	Access:

		Controller UI: http://localhost:8181

		Default credentials: admin/admin

6. Deploy Keycloak (Identity & Device Trust Anchor): Identity-based Zero Trust starts here.

				docker run -d \
				 --name keycloak \
				 -p 8080:8080 \
				 -e KEYCLOAK_ADMIN=admin \
				 -e KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin \
				 quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:latest start-dev


	Configure:

	Realm: SDP_ZeroTrust

	Clients: ODL-Client-A, ODL-Client-B

	Roles: trusted-device, untrusted-device, service-a, service-b

7. Deploy Open Policy Agent (Policy Engine):  Declarative, auditable trust logic.

				docker run -d \
				 --name opa \
				 -p 8182:8182 \
				 openpolicyagent/opa run --server


	Policies (example):	Identity claims, Device posture, Application sensitivity, Network context

	generate a rego script that grants access (full, limited and no access) based on 3 separate parameters: users for user categories admin, guest and blacklisted; devices for categories trusted and untrusted devices; and applications for types allowed and blocked applications. Generate the resulting json script as well. these two will be used in an open policy agent container

	rego script logic
	| User        | Device    | App     | Result      |
	| ----------- | --------- | ------- | ----------- |
	| Admin       | Trusted   | Allowed | **Full**    |
	| Admin       | Untrusted | Allowed | **Limited** |
	| Guest       | Trusted   | Allowed | **Limited** |
	| Guest       | Untrusted | Allowed | **None**    |
	| Any         | Any       | Blocked | **None**    |
	| Blacklisted | Any       | Any     | **None**    |


8. Deploy Envoy Proxy (Application PEP): Why: L7 Zero Trust enforcement.

				docker run -d \
				 --name envoy \
				 -p 10000:10000 \
				 envoyproxy/envoy:v1.30-latest


		Envoy integrates:

		OAuth2 (Keycloak)

		Policy checks (OPA)

9. Build the Mininet Zero Trust Topology: Minimal Topology

		Client

		Service-A

		Service-B

	OVS switch (controlled by OpenDaylight)

	sudo mn \
	 --topo single,3 \
	 --switch ovs \
	 --controller remote,ip=127.0.0.1,port=6653

